typedef struct __lock_t {
       int flag;

} lock_t;

void init(lock_t *lock) {

   // 0 indicates lock is available, 1 that it is held

   lock->flag = 0;

}                            Test-and-set is an atomic instruction

void lock(lock_t *lock) {

   while (TestAndSet(&lock->flag, 1) == 1); // spin-lock

} This is called “spin lock”

void unlock(lock_t *lock) {  spins using CPU cycles,
       lock->flag = 0;       until the lock becomes
                             available.
}

• As long as the lock is held by another thread, TestAndSet() will

   repeatedly return 1

• By making both the test (of the old value of the lock) and set (of the

   new value) a single atomic operation, we can ensure that only one

   thread acquires the lock

